  "reasoning": "This commit changed `parseRFC8601DateTime` (and its helper `getUS`) to return simulation time in seconds instead of microseconds/ticks, and updated all call sites (FileToArray.java, TimeSeriesDataInput.java) accordingly to stop dividing by 1e6. However, the two \"extended time\" branches (`isextendtime` and `isextendfull`, handling formats \"hh:mm:ss\" and \"hh:mm:ss.ssssss\") were left unchanged — they still compute `ret` in microseconds and `return ret;` directly, without converting to seconds like the rest of the function now does. This mismatch is exactly what the fix commit addresses by adding `* 1e-6` to those two return statements, converting the leftover-microsecond values to seconds to match the new function contract established in c374ff3ebc6d.",
